    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0542" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/979.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-02T22:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 2, 1913—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inflammatory speeches by opposition tonight precipitated conflict between
                    Government guards and the mob, causing several deaths and many wounded; there
                    were numerous arrests. Both sides are deaf to <pb facs="0543" n="439"
                        xml:id="pg439"/> reason and the time has arrived for positive action. The
                    Government seems determined to employ the old coercive measures and is
                    intolerant of criticism. I recommend that it be warned that the Department will
                    shut off revenues if force should be used to carry the election.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
